[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2831221427","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105763#issuecomment-2831221427","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105763","id":2831221427,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6owQKz","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-25T19:08:36Z","updated_at":"2025-04-25T19:08:36Z","body":"OmniLights and Spotlights cache their shadow maps, so shadows are only updated if an object in their view moves or is changed. That is expected behaviour and results from a pretty big optimization. \n\nWe should have better documentation about this though so it isn't so surprising. ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2831221427/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2831292145","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105763#issuecomment-2831292145","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105763","id":2831292145,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6owhbx","user":{"login":"Sr3qt","id":105977398,"node_id":"U_kgDOBlEWNg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105977398?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sr3qt","html_url":"https://github.com/Sr3qt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sr3qt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sr3qt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sr3qt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sr3qt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sr3qt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sr3qt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sr3qt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sr3qt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sr3qt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-25T19:40:08Z","updated_at":"2025-04-25T19:40:08Z","body":"I get that shadow maps would be cached, but after an object moves, why doesn't it re-cache the shadow maps while the objects are still in view of the camera? Why is it neccessary to look a away to re-cache them? Could it be made so it re-caches automatically?\n\nThanks for your response.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2831292145/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2831401904","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105763#issuecomment-2831401904","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105763","id":2831401904,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ow8Ow","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-25T20:46:53Z","updated_at":"2025-04-25T20:46:53Z","body":"> I get that shadow maps would be cached, but after an object moves, why doesn't it re-cache the shadow maps while the objects are still in view of the camera? Why is it neccessary to look a away to re-cache them? Could it be made so it re-caches automatically?\n\nIt does.\n\nIt updates every time something moves of is changed. If nothing moves and nothing changes, then it won't update. \n\nNaturally, that is an issue for games that require having shadowed objects that move within the frustum of the light every frame. For that we are exploring a way of updating the shadow map only for dynamic objects. ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2831401904/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3208963300","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105763#issuecomment-3208963300","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105763","id":3208963300,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6_ROTk","user":{"login":"jitspoe","id":7751182,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTExODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7751182?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe","html_url":"https://github.com/jitspoe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-21T04:34:02Z","updated_at":"2025-08-21T04:34:02Z","body":"I'm not able to reproduce this with the given MRP in my custom 4.5-ish build, but I'm definitely running into issues with my own project updating shadows when it shouldn't.  I disabled shadows on all the dynamic stuff (enemies, spinning pickups, etc.) and I'm still getting omni light shadow updates on all static geometry while standing still, as illustrated by this tracy capture:\n\n<img width=\"1451\" height=\"422\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/59ad8c24-2787-4273-9a47-00f7dd19116e\" />\n\nI have not been able to create a MRP project where this happens, though, so I'm not sure exactly what causes it.  I think there are some calls to make_shadow_dirty() on lights when there shouldn't be.  Unfortunately, large chunks of that code are force inlined, so I can put breakpoints and figure it out.  Hoping to track down some specifics so I can open an issue about it.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3208963300/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3209045552","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105763#issuecomment-3209045552","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105763","id":3209045552,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6_RiYw","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-21T05:25:26Z","updated_at":"2025-08-21T05:25:26Z","body":"@jitspoe if you compile without optimizations you won't have any inlining and can get accurate breakpoints anywhere","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3209045552/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3212835319","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105763#issuecomment-3212835319","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105763","id":3212835319,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6_f_n3","user":{"login":"jitspoe","id":7751182,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTExODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7751182?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe","html_url":"https://github.com/jitspoe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-22T02:36:46Z","updated_at":"2025-08-22T02:48:34Z","body":"That drastically changes the performance, though, so profiling isn't as useful.  I've temporarily commented out the force inline and tracked down the make dirty stuff:\n\n```\n>\tgodot.windows.editor.x86_64.exe!RendererSceneCull::_update_instance(RendererSceneCull::Instance * p_instance) Line 1707\tC++\n \tgodot.windows.editor.x86_64.exe!RendererSceneCull::_update_dirty_instance(RendererSceneCull::Instance * p_instance) Line 4151\tC++\n \t[Inline Frame] godot.windows.editor.x86_64.exe!RendererSceneCull::update_dirty_instances() Line 4158\tC++\n \tgodot.windows.editor.x86_64.exe!RendererSceneCull::update() Line 4178\tC++\n \tgodot.windows.editor.x86_64.exe!RenderingServerDefault::_draw(bool p_swap_buffers, double frame_step) Line 87\tC++\n \tgodot.windows.editor.x86_64.exe!RenderingServerDefault::draw(bool p_present, double frame_step) Line 430\tC++\n \tgodot.windows.editor.x86_64.exe!Main::iteration() Line 4820\tC++\n \tgodot.windows.editor.x86_64.exe!OS_Windows::run() Line 2255\tC++\n```\n\nI have a pretty simple scene with nothing moving, yet 2 omni lights are updating.\n\n<img width=\"1920\" height=\"1040\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7b484f16-ba5f-493f-8721-bcf3c2eb75a1\" />\n\nI had a monster in the scene then deleted it.\n\nIt seems like maybe the dirty flag is never clearing for some geometry and it's just forcing updates every frame.  Still digging into it.\n\nThis is where the light is made dirty:\n```c++\nvoid RendererSceneCull::_update_instance(Instance *p_instance) const {\n...\n\tif ((1 << p_instance->base_type) & RS::INSTANCE_GEOMETRY_MASK) {\n\t\tInstanceGeometryData *geom = static_cast<InstanceGeometryData *>(p_instance->base_data);\n\t\t//make sure lights are updated if it casts shadow\n\n\t\tif (geom->can_cast_shadows) {\n\t\t\tfor (const Instance *E : geom->lights) {\n\t\t\t\tInstanceLightData *light = static_cast<InstanceLightData *>(E->base_data);\n\t\t\t\tlight->make_shadow_dirty();\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n```\n\n\nEdit: I think it might be due to rigid bodies.  Even though they're asleep and not moving, removing them from the radius of the omni light seems to have stopped the updates.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3212835319/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3212871737","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105763#issuecomment-3212871737","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105763","id":3212871737,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6_gIg5","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-22T03:02:59Z","updated_at":"2025-08-22T03:02:59Z","body":"Hmmmm rigid body must update something that triggers an instance update even when sleeping. \n\nWe should track it down and see if it's a necessary update or not. Perhaps this is a bug in rigid body","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3212871737/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3212918367","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105763#issuecomment-3212918367","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105763","id":3212918367,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6_gT5f","user":{"login":"jitspoe","id":7751182,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTExODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7751182?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe","html_url":"https://github.com/jitspoe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jitspoe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-22T03:36:04Z","updated_at":"2025-08-22T04:14:43Z","body":"Of course it wouldn't be as simple as just having a rigid body near an omni light.  Tried to do a MRP for that and it won't repro.  I don't know why KOOK seems to dig up so many light bugs that I can't reproduce in simpler scenes. :(\n\nEdit: It seems like it was the Godot plush, which has multiple rigid bodies and 6dof joints so the arms and legs can flop around.  I guess it never quite goes to sleep.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3212918367/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]